<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67551" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆτις</span></b> , ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			3.9
		</span></i>; acc. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτιας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ven.</u>
					249
				</span></i>
			; also gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				61
			</span></i> (lyr.); acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδας</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				626
			</span></i> (lyr.); dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτιδι</span> Orac.
				ap.<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.141
			</span></i>; 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτῑ</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτιϊ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (v. infr.); pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητίεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			; acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆτιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.407
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				158
			</span></i> (lyr.):—<i>wisdom, skill, craft</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὶ μῆτιν ἀτάλαντος</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητίετα</span>) Il.l.c., al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροτείη μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν Διὸς γὰρ οὐχ ὁρῶ μῆτιν, ὅπᾳ
					φύγοιμ᾽ ἄν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					906
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτι . . καὶ κέρδεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.299
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτι . . μέγ᾽ ἀμείνων ἠὲ βίηφι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.315
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆτιν ἀλώπηξ</span> a fox
				<i>for craft</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				4(3).47
			</span></i>; of a poet's <i>craft</i>, Id.<u>N.</u>l.c.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>counsel, plan, undertaking</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφαίνειν μῆτιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.324
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.678
			</span></i>, etc.: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφῶν μητίεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικοβούλους μήτιδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c.— Poet. word. (Cf. Skt.
			<i>mimāti</i>, pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			<i>mitá</i>- 'measure', Lat. <i>metior</i>, O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>mæþ</i> 'measure'.)</div>
